; One variable: a quad whose top and bottom edges sit on pixel centres in y (100.5, 300.5, 300.5).
; Godot's top-left rule draws the top row and skips the bottom row, so a 96 px quad at y = 100.5
; covers rows 100 to 195. WholePixel keeps its edges between centres and draws the same 96 rows.
